{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nOperator-declared serious bug: the review-bot's LLM-Review vote publishes only a COUNT of\nadvisory findings (\"PASS. N advisory finding(s) (non-blocking)\"), and the finding TEXT is\nretrievable nowhere on the Gerrit change. Operator impact, verbatim: \"if they're invisible it\nmakes it difficult for us to determine which advisory findings should be promoted to blocking.\"\nThis feeds the pending blocking-lane re-enable work.\n\n## Root cause (AC1 — CONFIRMED, see ticket comment #1 for full evidence)\n\nPremise correction: the behaviour is NOT inconsistent. Advisory text is published on NO change.\nChange 1636 is not a counter-example — live Gerrit shows `revisions/current/comments` = `{}` and\n`robotcomments` = \"robot comments unsupported\" for 1636, 1666 AND 1685 alike, and all three\ncarry the same count-only bot message.\n\nMechanism, single and deterministic:\n1. `src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py:132` `_summarize()`, PASS branch (lines 134-138) renders only\n   `len(verdict[\"advisory\"])`. It never itemises the findings.\n2. The `\"finding\"` branch (lines 139-152) itemises BLOCKING findings only — advisory text is\n   dropped there too, so a BLOCK vote hides advisories as well.\n3. `_translate_findings` (`adapter.py:114`) copies `{severity, dimension, detail}` and DISCARDS\n   each finding's `location`, so no file/line anchor ever reaches the Gerrit layer.\n4. `voter.py:700` calls `gc.post_vote(change_id, revision, value, message)` — four positional\n   args — so `post_vote`'s `robot_comments` parameter (`gerrit_client.py:277-294`) is never\n   supplied in production and always falls back to one `/PATCHSET_LEVEL` robot comment carrying\n   the same message string. No code path builds a per-file comment map.\n\nRejected hypotheses: posting failure / auth (the vote POST succeeds — LLM-Review+1 landed on all\nthree) and a size or count threshold (the count is unbounded).\n\nEnvironmental constraint the fix must respect: robot comments are DISABLED on this Gerrit server,\nso the review message body is the only surface proven to render. Body enumeration is therefore\nthe guaranteed surface; inline comments are additive.\n\n## Plan\n\nNew module `src/rebar/review_bot/finding_publish.py` (keeps `voter.py`, currently 778 LOC, under\nthe 800 cap):\n- `parse_anchor(location)` — split a free-text `location` into `(path, line|None)`, tolerating\n  a missing or non-numeric line tail; `None` when there is no usable path.\n- `partition_findings(findings, revision_paths)` — anchorable only when the parsed path is a\n  real path in the revision's file map; everything else is anchor-less.\n- `render_findings_block(findings, kind)` — enumerated `- (criterion) detail [location]` lines,\n  per-line truncation, and an explicit \"N additional ... omitted\" overflow note.\n- `build_inline_comments(anchorable)` — `{path: [{line, message, unresolved: false}]}`.\n  `unresolved: false` keeps the \"no unresolved comments\" submit requirement untouched.\n\n`adapter.py`:\n- `_translate_findings` also carries `location` through (additive key; existing consumers of\n  `{severity, dimension, detail}` are unaffected).\n- `_summarize` PASS branch keeps the existing count sentence and APPENDS the enumerated advisory\n  block. The `\"finding\"` branch appends the advisory block after the blocking list.\n\n`gerrit_client.post_vote`: accept an optional `comments` mapping and include it in the review\nbody when non-empty. The existing `robot_comments` default is unchanged (AC5).\n\n`voter.py` (minimal delta at the `post_vote` call site, ~line 700): best-effort fetch of the\nrevision file map to validate anchors (any failure degrades to zero anchorable findings, i.e.\nbody-only); post with `comments`; on `GerritError` from the comment-bearing POST, retry\nmessage-only with an appended notice naming the ticket's REVIEW_RESULT sidecar as the full\nrecord (AC3).\n\nDesign tradeoff, stated deliberately: EVERY advisory is enumerated in the message body, and\nanchorable ones are ALSO posted inline. Duplication is cheap; invisibility is the bug, and the\nbody is the only surface this server is proven to render.\n\n## Testing\n\nRun from the worktree venv: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_review_bot.py tests/unit/test_review_bot_finding_publish.py -q`,\nthen `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` and `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`.\nEach AC4 sub-case is a named test in `tests/unit/test_review_bot_finding_publish.py`, RED-verified\nby running it against unpatched `main` first.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 — Root cause identified and recorded as a ticket comment (checked: comment #1 cites the live `GET /a/changes/<n>/revisions/current/comments` and `/robotcomments` responses), with the operator's\n  \"1636 is a counter-example\" premise corrected against live Gerrit API state.\n- [ ] AC2 — Every advisory finding is retrievable from the Gerrit change: enumerated in the\n  review message body on both the PASS and the BLOCK path, and additionally posted as an inline\n  comment when its location anchors to a real path in the revision.\n- [ ] AC3 — A comment-posting failure is never silent: the vote still lands, and its message\n  carries an explicit notice that inline publication failed and that the full finding set lives\n  in the ticket's REVIEW_RESULT sidecar.\n- [ ] AC4 — Regression tests pin: (a) advisory findings appear as text in the PASS message\n  (the reproduced 1666/1685 condition — RED against current main, which emits a count only);\n  (b) advisory text also appears on the BLOCK path; (c) an anchorable finding produces an inline\n  comment keyed by path with `unresolved: false`; (d) an anchor-less or off-revision finding is\n  still enumerated in the body and produces no inline comment; (e) a `GerritError` on the\n  comment-bearing POST falls back to a message-only vote carrying the failure notice.\n- [ ] AC5 — `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` and `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck` pass; no change to vote semantics — label name,\n  vote values, PASS/BLOCK mapping, fail-closed coverage-gap behaviour and the dedup/retry\n  bookkeeping are all untouched."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786574819671226001,"uuid":"2cb6b3f9-5019-44a9-8ca2-873df32e11cc"}